      "title": "All imports (l–w)",
      "items": [
        "lineage: auth, kpis, sources, warehouse, workspaces",
        "llm: activity, audit, auth, workspaces",
        "mail: auth, workspaces",
        "memory: auth, changesets, sources, workspaces",
        "notifications: auth",
        "propagation: audit, auth, changesets, kpis, notifications, warehouse, workspaces",
        "sources: activity, audit, auth, changesets, jobs, notifications, workspaces",
        "warehouse: activity, audit, auth, changesets, notifications, sources, workspaces",
        "web: audit, auth, workspaces",
        "workspaces: activity, audit, auth, notifications"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Runtime ports wired by composition roots (not imports)",
      "items": [
        "workspaces archive → jobs.cancel_for_workspace + changesets.reject_pending (app.state.on_workspace_archived, app.py:203-211).",
        "sources new Snapshot → warehouse staging sync + regeneration offer (wiring.staging_sync_after_snapshot).",
        "structural change / accepted Change Set → propagation (wiring.propagation, after_change_set).",
        "llm embedding model changed → files.start_reembed; workspaces created → llm.on_workspace_created; auth → mail through the Mailer port.",
        "Change Set object handlers from sources, warehouse, kpis, memory, files registered in wiring.change_set_handlers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Enforced rules",
      "items": [
        "Import another module only through its package; tables are private (modules/README.md rules 1-5).",
        "tools/check_boundaries.py (CI) checks rule 1, part of rule 2, and rule 3; raw SQL on other modules' tables is left to review."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Uncertain",
      "items": [
        "Imports were collected with a text search for `from dawam.modules.<name>` and `from dawam.modules import`; imports inside functions are included, dynamic imports are not.",
        "An import does not prove a runtime call on every path; the diagram is a static dependency map."
      ]
    }
